---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "../components/Breadcrumbs.astro";
import { site } from "../data/site";
---

<BaseLayout title="Terms of use" description="Terms for quotations, orders, artwork, payment, delivery and defects on custom labels and stickers, including the limits of what we can reprint.">
  <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: "Terms" }]} />
  <section class="tight">
    <div class="wrap narrow prose">
      <h1>Terms of use</h1>
      <p class="small">Last updated: November 2026</p>

      <h2>Quotations and orders</h2>
      <p>Prices are quoted per project and are valid for 30 days unless stated otherwise. A quotation is not an order; production only begins after written approval of the artwork proof and receipt of the deposit stated in the quotation. An order is accepted when we confirm it in writing and the deposit clears. These terms apply to that order unless we agree different terms in writing.</p>

      <h2>Minimum order</h2>
      <p>{site.moq} units per design. Multiple designs may be combined in one order where material, size and finishing match.</p>

      <h2>Artwork and intellectual property</h2>
      <p>You confirm that you own or are licensed to use everything you send us, including logos, fonts and images. We use your artwork only to produce your order and will not resell or reuse the design. Files we prepare (proofs, dielines) remain our working documents; the design remains yours.</p>
      <p>We keep approved artwork for the production period and, unless you ask us to delete it, for a reasonable reorder window so a repeat order can skip the setup. We do not publish your artwork, brand or order details without written permission. If your artwork contains personal data (for example, a signature or a photograph), tell us before sending it so we can handle it accordingly.</p>

      <h2>Proofs and approval</h2>
      <p>You are responsible for checking the proof: spelling, size, colour, barcode data and legal text. Once approved in writing, the proof becomes the production specification. Colour may vary slightly between screens, proofing methods and production runs; where an exact match is required, it must be agreed in writing before production.</p>

      <h2>Payment</h2>
      <p>Terms are stated in the quotation. Production starts after the deposit clears; the balance is due before dispatch unless credit terms are agreed in writing. This website does not process card payments. Bank charges levied by intermediary banks are the buyer’s responsibility unless the quotation says otherwise.</p>

      <h2>Delivery and risk</h2>
      <p>Lead times are estimates made in good faith and depend on artwork approval and carrier performance. Risk passes according to the shipping terms in the quotation. Import duties and taxes are the buyer's responsibility unless the quotation states otherwise. If a shipment is delayed, damaged or short, tell us within seven days of delivery so we can open the carrier claim; production defects are handled under the 14-day window below.</p>

      <h2>Inspection and claims</h2>
      <p>Tell us within 14 days of delivery, with photos, if goods are defective or do not match the approved proof. Transit damage or a short delivery must be reported within seven days, so the carrier claim can be opened in time. We will reprint, credit or refund at our option. We are not liable for defects caused by artwork we were asked to print as supplied, or by misuse after delivery. Where the remedy is a reprint, the affected quantity must be made available for inspection or photographs, and we will confirm the remedy in writing before reprinting.</p>

      <h2>Liability</h2>
      <p>Our liability for any order is limited to the value of that order. We are not liable for indirect or consequential loss, including lost sales or delayed launches. Nothing in these terms excludes liability that cannot be excluded by law.</p>

      <h2>Force majeure</h2>
      <p>We are not liable for a delay or failure caused by an event outside our reasonable control, including carrier disruption, customs action, a public holiday, a shortage of a specific material, or a government restriction. If such an event occurs, we will tell you promptly and agree a revised schedule or a cancellation of the unaffected part of the order.</p>

      <h2>Governing law and disputes</h2>
      <p>These terms are governed by the laws applicable at the seller's place of business. The parties will first try to resolve a dispute by good-faith negotiation; if that fails, the courts at the seller’s place of business have jurisdiction, unless a mandatory consumer-protection rule says otherwise. The contract is between business parties; consumer cancellation rights do not apply to custom-printed goods.</p>

      <h2>Entire agreement</h2>
      <p>These terms, the quotation and the approved proof form the whole agreement for the order. A statement made in an email or chat that is not repeated in those documents does not override them. If any provision is unenforceable, the rest remains in force.</p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p><a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
